; Leg EK -- EDIT 26 REGRESSION.  Server mode; this side drives.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
;  REMOTE HELP IS FIRST, DELIBERATELY (SS16ax): before concluding a
;  feature does not work, check that the thing asking for it can ask.
;
;  REMOTE DIRECTORY walks A:'s 184 root entries through snddir(), which
;  is the function edit 26 touched.  SS16aw listed 157 entries in
;  31.077 s with the debug log SHUT; this leg has no -d.
;
;  ">" REDIRECTS ARE REQUIRED, not stylistic: this bench's older client
;  fell off an empty argument in remcfm() (SS16ax).  Use "remote pwd >
;  file", never bare "remote pwd".
;
;  FINISH, not BYE -- BYE would stop the server and SS16ax leg SA lost
;  its whole .OUT to a terminating command that killed the channel the
;  leg reported through.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPEK.OUT> s16bdEK.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 9600
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bdEK.pkt
remote help > s16bdEK-help.txt
remote pwd > s16bdEK-pwd.txt
remote directory > s16bdEK-dir.txt
remote space > s16bdEK-space.txt
finish
statistics
